{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"JLSEC-2026-1263","published":"2026-08-12T15:58:36.032Z","modified":"2026-11-20T14:15:02.385621652Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-13595"],"details":"A flaw was found in the libblkid library of util-linux. During nested partition probing, the BSD, Minix, Solaris x86, and UnixWare partition probers cache a raw pointer to a parent partition entry in a dynamically allocated array. When subsequent partition additions cause the array to be reallocated, this pointer becomes stale, leading to a heap use-after-free read. An attacker who can present a crafted block device image (for example, via USB insertion or a loop-mounted disk image) can trigger this flaw without user interaction, as libblkid is invoked automatically by udev/udisks as root on block-device hot-plug events. This could lead to limited information disclosure or denial of service.","affected":[{"package":{"name":"Libmount_jll","ecosystem":"Julia","purl":"pkg:julia/Libmount_jll?uuid=4b2f31a3-9ecc-558c-b454-b3730dcb73e9"},"ranges":[{"type":"SEMVER","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"2.42.2+0"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/JuliaLang/SecurityAdvisories.jl/tree/generated/osv/2026/JLSEC-2026-1263.json"}},{"package":{"name":"util_linux_jll","ecosystem":"Julia","purl":"pkg:julia/util_linux_jll?uuid=a762b42e-dc87-5958-a639-9c9eec9c0153"},"ranges":[{"type":"SEMVER","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"2.42.4+0"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/JuliaLang/SecurityAdvisories.jl/tree/generated/osv/2026/JLSEC-2026-1263.json"}}],"references":[{"type":"WEB","url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:26573"},{"type":"WEB","url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:93461"},{"type":"WEB","url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:95365"},{"type":"WEB","url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:96212"},{"type":"WEB","url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:97522"},{"type":"WEB","url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:99119"},{"type":"WEB","url":"https://access.redhat.com/security/cve/CVE-2026-13595"},{"type":"WEB","url":"https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=2494101"},{"type":"WEB","url":"https://github.com/util-linux/util-linux/commit/c0186f14fbdb02f64c8e0ba701ce727ea764ff4c"}],"database_specific":{"license":"CC-BY-4.0","sources":[{"affected":{"kernel:util-linux":["< 2.42.2"]},"database_specific":{"status":"Modified"},"html_url":"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-13595","id":"CVE-2026-13595","imported":"2026-11-20T04:52:39.563Z","modified":"2026-11-12T11:17:11.967Z","published":"2026-06-29T09:16:28.303Z","url":"https://services.nvd.nist.gov/rest/json/cves/2.0?cveId=CVE-2026-13595"}]},"severity":[{"type":"CVSS_V3","score":"CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:H/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:N/A:H","source":"NVD"}]}